From: ArchPad project <archpad@localhost>
Subject: media: i2c: hi846: assert reset while acquiring GPIO

HI846 RESETB is active low.  Requesting the GPIO with GPIOD_OUT_LOW
deasserts reset immediately, before the sensor supplies and input clock are
enabled.  The later power-on sequence only writes the same deasserted state,
so a warm probe does not produce a reset pulse and the sensor can stop
acknowledging I2C transfers.

Acquire the reset GPIO asserted.  hi846_power_on() already deasserts it after
enabling the supplies and clock, while hi846_power_off() asserts it before
turning them off.

---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -2058,7 +2058,7 @@ static int hi846_parse_dt(struct hi846 *hi846, struct device *dev)
 
 	v4l2_fwnode_endpoint_free(&bus_cfg);
 
-	hi846->rst_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	hi846->rst_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_HIGH);
 	if (IS_ERR(hi846->rst_gpio)) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to get reset gpio: %pe\n",
 			hi846->rst_gpio);
